#basePath	Day3

:: BeginDay
@trigger    SceneReady
@boostScore 100
@who    Astrid

$call InitUpdateMasks()
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(CoordinateInstrument, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(PhotometerInstrument, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(BlueWavelength, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(ColorInstrument, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(TemperatureInstrument, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(SpectrometerInstrument, true)
$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 40)
$call StopPuzzleMode()
$call StopOpenMode()

$call MoveToView("DocumentPuzzle")
$call SetInputState(false)
$call SpawnDocumentToCamera("MiniLabors")
$call SetInputState(true)

:: SpawnPuzzleDocs1
@trigger    DocumentInspectEnd
@when   documentId == "MiniLabors"
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
$call Wait(1)

$call SpawnDocumentToCamera("Day3ElijahPostcard")
$call SetInputState(true)

:: Day3ElijahPostcardFlavor
@trigger    DocumentInspectFlip
@when   documentId == "Day3ElijahPostcard"
@cutscene
@once

{@Astrid} I don’t get it. We need to warn people? About what?
{@Astrid} Ugh. Elijah, I love you, but I could really use less poetry and more information. 

:: SpawnPuzzleDocs2
@trigger    DocumentInspectEnd
@when   documentId == "Day3ElijahPostcard"
@interrupt
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
$call Wait(1)
$call SpawnDocumentToCamera("HerculesPostcard")
$call SetInputState(true)

:: SpawnPuzzleDocs3
@trigger    DocumentInspectEnd
@when   documentId == "HerculesPostcard"
@interrupt
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
$call Wait(1)
$call StartDocumentPuzzle("Day3DocumentPuzzle")
$call SetInputState(true)
{@Astrid} Has Elijah gone crazy? 

:: IncorrectDocumentResponse
@trigger    DocumentPuzzlePromptStart
@when   documentId != "HerculesPostcard"
@interrupt

NO.

:: CorrectDocumentResponse
@trigger    DocumentPuzzlePromptStart
@when   documentId == "HerculesPostcard"
@cutscene
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
{@Astrid} Yeah, that looks like it. $[Day3/Astrid/a_confirm_1]
$call Wait(1)

$call SetInputState(false)
$call MoveToView("Right")
$call Wait(1)

{@Dad} Astrid, this is Ursa Major. Great job identifying Hercules! 
{@Dad} I got your letter about Elijah, and all those cryptic notes you found.  
{@Dad} I’m sorry, kiddo, but I don’t know much more than you do. 
{@Dad} A few months ago, Elijah mentioned some kind of secret project he was working on.
{@Dad} He said it was a big deal. But you know Elijah. Everything’s a big deal to him. 
{@Dad} He’s always been a dreamer . .  . I could see it even when you were kids.
{@Dad} I think sometimes he forgets people can’t read his mind. 
{@Dad} There could be a logical explanation. Elijah doesn’t seem like the type to go off the deep end.
{@Dad} But then again, these are strange times.  

{@Astrid} Oookay. I gotta be honest, Dad. That’s not exactly comforting. 

{@Dad} For now, why don’t you keep exploring? I’ll let you know when we’ve got your next assignment. 
{@Dad} And in the meantime, I’ll see if I can find out more about Elijah. 
{@Dad} Love you, Little Bear.

{@Astrid} Love you, Dad. Sure wish you could hear me. 

{@Radio} Star HQ to Station Seven. IceCube is reading a high-energy neutrino emission from the area of the Orion Constellation.
{@Radio} Identification of nearby celestial objects is requested. Uploading area of interest...
$call StartNeutrinoNavigation()
$call SetInputState(true)

:: NeutrinoNavigationComplete
@trigger    NeutrinoNavigationComplete
@once

$call StopNeutrinoNavigation()
{@Radio} Neutrino Origin Detected
$call StartOpenMode()

:: PointsUpdated
@trigger    PointsUpdated
@when   sciencePoints > 2
@cutscene
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
$call SetRefGuideActive(false)

$call Wait(3)

$call StopOpenMode()
$call ClearMonitorSelection()

$call MonitorUI->PlayRadioDownload(2)
$call Wait(1)
$call MonitorUI->ShowCeresLogo()
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(HistoricalDataInstrument, true)
{@Radio} Congratulations on being awarded clearance level 4. You are now cleared to use the historical data module.
{@Radio} Please reference your CERES Operator Manual for further information about your equipment.  $[Day3/Radio/l1_r_3(2)]
{@Radio} Thanking you for being an important part of the CERES Distributed Network of Citizen Observatories. Together, we will map the stars for a better tomorrow. $[Day3/Radio/l1_r_3(3)]
$call Wait(0.5)
{@Radio} Tuning you to the Ice Cube CERES headquarters for further instruction... $[Day3/Radio/l1_r_4]
$call MonitorUI->HideCeresLogo()
$call Wait(1)
$call StartPuzzleNavigation()
$call SetInputState(true)

:: PuzzleNavigationComplete
@trigger    PuzzleNavigationComplete
@once

$call StopPuzzleNavigation()
$call StartPuzzleMode()

:: LeoPuzzleComplete
@trigger    CorrectPuzzleSubmission
@when   puzzleName == "Leo"
@cutscene
@once

$call ClearMonitorSelection()
$call StopPuzzleMode()
$call SetInputState(false)
$set temp:d3PostcardRead = false
$call SpawnDocumentToCamera("Day41833")
$call SetInputState(true)

:: Flip1833
@trigger    DocumentInspectFlip
@when   documentId == "Day41833"
@cutscene
@interrupt
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
{@Astrid} Whoa. There was a huge Leonid meteor storm in 1833! People thought the world was ending. Does Elijah think it’s going to happen again?
{@Astrid} If this is true, people won’t understand what’s happening. Everyone’s gonna panic. 

{@Astrid} Okay. We could write to the newspaper and tell people what’s happening, but first we need to know when and where the meteor storm will happen.
$call SetInputState(true)
$set temp:d3PostcardRead = true

:: End1833
@trigger    DocumentInspectEnd
@when   documentId == "Day41833", temp:d3PostcardRead
@interrupt
@once

$call LoadNextDay()